That sounds vaguely similar to my most recent game (as a caveman) ...
It started off well. I did the first few levels, found a ghost with a 
rusty long sword which soon became Excalibur, and got down to mine town.
In mine town, the lighting store had 4 lamps and only 3 candles. No problem,
says I, by the time I need candles I'll have a wand of wishing. A few
levels down I find a lamp which isn't named "oil" and soon have myself
some nice Gray Dragon Scale Mail. I continue onward until I reach Mr. Castle.
I wade through an incredible variety of nasty critters and get mr. wand of
wishing. (Along the way I found 2 amulets of life saving, so I'm pretty safe).
I pile up 2 armies worth of armor, wish for a wand of polymorph, and soon 
have speed boots, gauntlets of power, helm of telepathy, cloak of displacement
and shield of reflection. After wandering down into the valley of death,
I'm finally level 14 and ready for my quest. Well, as some of you certainly
know, the caveman quest takes place in a dungeon where some spaces can't
be walked through (since they're diagonal) unless you aren't carrying very
much, and the walls can't be dug to widen the passage. So, I decide to stick
everything in my bag of holding, so I won't be carrying as much. Do I have any
wands of cancellation? Yes, I have two. I drop them. Do I have any other
bags of holding? No. So I should be find. apply mr. bag and stick in "a". 
WHAT????? A bag of TRICKS caused a magical explosion????
Well, goodbye bag of holding. It contained, among other things,
my backup AoLS, 2 wands of polymorph, +3 Mjollnir (from a ghost), 
+/- 50 food rations, 10 or so potions of holy water, my tinning kit, 
a wand of wishing WITH ONLY ONE WISH USED!!!!!, my boots of water walking
(for making potions of water) and a bunch of other stuff. The only blessing
was that my Excalibur was later in my inventory than the bag of tricks, so
I wasn't unarmed. To make a long story short, I found a bunch more food,
killed the Chromatic dragon, got a cursed bell of opening and got up to
30th level, and cleaned house in Gehennom. But we have two other plot elements
to remember: (1) I only had 3 candles, and no wands of wishing or polymorph to
make more. and (2) the entire game I NEVER EVER FOUND A SCROLL OF GENOCIDE 
meaning that I still had master liches, minotaurs, cockatrices, etc. running
around. I had plenty of magic markers to make myself lots of scrolls of
genocide, but I COULDN'T!

Also, I was out of amulets of life saving. I lost one in my bag, one from
choking on a FORTUNE COOKIE. (I didn't even know they had any food value
at all, much less enough to make you choke to death without warning) and
one from polymorphing into a rust monster (to eat my ring of polymorph control) and being ambushed my a minotaur.
You return to human form... well, no time to put my armor on, I know, I've
got a scroll of taming in my new bag of holding, I'll just whip that baby otu
and... die before reading it.

In any case, I spent 20 or 30 thousand turns wandering around killing
random generated monsters before I got a wand of polymorph. I then went
through the entire dungeon collecting and lugging tools until I had 
3 pages of them, and polypiled until I got enough candles, killed Mr. high
priest, got the amulet, went back up (despite Mr. Wizard who refused to
stop coming back even after being polymorphed and/or stoned several times),
stopped for 15000 more turns to make myself some holy water (my god was
displeased with me, and then he was so pleased with me that he made me
the hand of elbereth... ???? ) and headed upward to the elemental planes,
which were a cinch because I met NO ARCHONS at all. Why? Beats me. In any 
case, I got up to the astral plane, was wanering around killing things
to my hearts content, until I met Pestilence. I killed him. He came back
to life, reached out with his deadly touch, and I was deadly ill. No problem,
I have a lump of royal jelly in my bag of holding. But do I survive the one
turn it takes to get it out (I had stopped carrying it in my inventory after
killing jubilex and seeing orcus bite the dust). Bye bye Buford the
cave man. Died in the end game about 4 steps from the altar with the
amulet (and never once did he see a scroll of genocide).

Part of that was due to my impatience and ignorance, but still!

Oh well, at least it didn't happen the _first_ time I got to the endgame
(I ascended with a valk after wading through no fewer than 37 archons) or
I would have shot myself

